aniser.org/2026/08/25/376941/bharat/keralam-muslim-youth-participate-in-onam-celebrations-despite-islamic-fundamentalist-opposition/", "summary": "Muslim women and students in Kerala participate in Onam celebrations in schools, colleges and public programmes. They view it as a cultural event rather than a religious ritual. This active participation happens despite occasional cautions, opposition and even fatwas from fundamentalist Islamic clerics. Onam is widely accepted in Kerala as a statewide harvest festival. In addition to Hindus, Muslim students, both boys and girls quite often join campus festivities wearing traditional attire, the Onam costumes. They join other students in making floral carpets (Pookkalam) and participating in cultural programmes such as Thiruvathira dance. Videos of hijab-wearing girls dancing at school Onam functions go viral on social media. These entertainments may contribute towards religious harmony. However, there are arguments for and against such participation on social media. The Islamic fundamentalists have historically discouraged this. They view Onam celebrations as contrary to Islamic the...", "published_at": "2026-08-25 11:30:45+00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Organiser", "tier": "independent", "url": "https://organiser.org"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 90, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 12, "confidence": 0.284, "rationale": "\"{\\\"framing\\\": {\\\"connotation_score\\\": 6.2, \\\"keyword_emphasis_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"omission_score\\\": 40.0, \\\"headline_body_divergence\\\": 18.4, \\\"has_cluster_context\\\": true}}\""}]}}, {"article": {"id": "0999b9f5-85b3-4c8f-9d4d-6e564809d29a", "title": "Union Minister Suresh Gopi Gives Rs 32 Lakh from Personal Funds to Clear Kudumbashree Workers’ Unpaid Onam Wages", "url": "https://organiser.org/2026/08/24/376757/bharat/union-minister-suresh-gopi-gives-rs-32-lakh-from-personal-funds-to-clear-kudumbashree-workers-unpaid-onam-wages/", "summary": "Union Minister Suresh Gopi offered Rs 32 lakh on August 22 to clear four to five months of pending wages owed to Kudumbashree women workers deployed under the Tourism Department in Alappuzha. The move was intended to ensure that the workers could celebrate Onam with their families without financial hardship. Gopi said the amount would be provided as an advance and refunded once the government released the pending funds. However, officials later confirmed that the government had sanctioned the dues and initiated the process to clear the payments. Kudumbashree is a major poverty-reduction and women’s empowerment programme run by the Kerala Government. Launched in 1997, it brings millions of women into local self-help groups aimed at promoting financial independence, small businesses and community development. The Kudumbashree workers deployed under the Tourism Department in Alappuzha had reportedly gone without wages for four to five months. The total pending amount was around Rs 32 l...", "published_at": "2026-08-24 10:50:29+00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Organiser", "tier": "independent", "url": "https://organiser.org"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 50, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 9, "confidence": 0.7, "rationale": "\"{\\\"framing\\\": {\\\"connotation_score\\\": 12.5, \\\"keyword_emphasis_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"omission_score\\\": 40.0, \\\"headline_body_divergence\\\": 1.4, \\\"has_cluster_context\\\": true}}\""}]}}]